<code>assert (0 <= index && index <= size) => (element == null) || (this.get(index).equals(element));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert (0 <= index && index <= this.size()) => (element == null) || (this.get(index).equals(element));</code>

However, the above assertion might not be entirely accurate because the `add` method shifts elements to the right, so the element at the specified index after the addition will be the newly added element, not necessarily the same as the element that was there before. The correct assertion should reflect that the element at the specified index after the addition is the newly added element.

Therefore, the correct assert statement should be:

<code>assert (0 <= index && index <= this.size()) => this.get(index).equals(element);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert (0 <= index && index <= this.size()) => (element == null ? this.get(index) == null : this.get(index).equals(element));</code>
--------------------
